[{:db/id "q-15323/selection/8747571c5bfc3ec50ef90efe2dbdc6a3bc073ec1be0dd315aa12a6433ca3345d" :answer/id #uuid "381b9ca1-a5af-5b6c-8a29-66b6b624124f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15323/selection/d09fcc5c04955b4f0467ac1dba0a88f70432fcff7629f87ea1957530ff9b8841" :answer/id #uuid "96b9e163-dc2d-5547-b450-c946fe7dabf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15323/selection/cbc4e187b2ebd68afcd828e04c9ab102796dd48ed6f097171966f76a9f8bc623" :answer/id #uuid "96c64803-628d-594f-b58f-98a5c8c014c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+x}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15323/selection/af6a17b410251a9b2c880bc4617c4c19e71ddd64dda2f7b850f53dbfc8c847d1" :answer/id #uuid "3a169470-f318-584a-bfb0-d0ba0ccf0484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15323/selection/30759faa981004f4a845018305cd97b05b3df401f1af5f03828f351be9981bc8" :answer/id #uuid "0fac23b7-e567-57d0-bd41-68f565981d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{ln}^{2}⁡x}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15323/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c511cec6-3e20-558b-915d-99f55368802d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15323/selection/d09fcc5c04955b4f0467ac1dba0a88f70432fcff7629f87ea1957530ff9b8841" :answer-field/choices ["q-15323/selection/8747571c5bfc3ec50ef90efe2dbdc6a3bc073ec1be0dd315aa12a6433ca3345d" "q-15323/selection/d09fcc5c04955b4f0467ac1dba0a88f70432fcff7629f87ea1957530ff9b8841" "q-15323/selection/cbc4e187b2ebd68afcd828e04c9ab102796dd48ed6f097171966f76a9f8bc623" "q-15323/selection/af6a17b410251a9b2c880bc4617c4c19e71ddd64dda2f7b850f53dbfc8c847d1" "q-15323/selection/30759faa981004f4a845018305cd97b05b3df401f1af5f03828f351be9981bc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15323" :question/id #uuid "676c520e-2bd4-5a9f-a56a-7aedf1c83e6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-15323" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ on $[1,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $a=1,$ and $b=2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15323/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15323"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984/selection/c8f62f06e171df6e3f636b9c43ad430937d6c62c4b881979c6711a7c388f3387" :answer/id #uuid "fcce3f8a-e74f-5250-9691-e7b13f82c71e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984/selection/f8637ee93997845fe7856013ddf80bbbf6faa8559d2416f05f41bda15c3b0694" :answer/id #uuid "9632369b-eb7a-5e68-894e-d9071e3485ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984/selection/f9d04c9c9aebd95d4a5851eca34c20e710d86597253d39199142f142ece1434f" :answer/id #uuid "4d078cc5-0265-52d9-81b0-8d51d81385ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984/selection/f49e5f4b6fe6e1c12a4d7501c2392108e0d059370f9e53e2fc0e117cf664fa60" :answer/id #uuid "44237b70-f068-5b2e-bc85-b7f7e868b999" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984/selection/fe02abcadda6602139249542e8243f50894f0a42aacae4c0c9af2555f94d3639" :answer/id #uuid "c32a732c-57f3-5692-8181-a4342258fe61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4f98978-f5bb-5067-9b81-51c09b8ac739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-5984/selection/c8f62f06e171df6e3f636b9c43ad430937d6c62c4b881979c6711a7c388f3387" :answer-field/choices ["q-5984/selection/c8f62f06e171df6e3f636b9c43ad430937d6c62c4b881979c6711a7c388f3387" "q-5984/selection/f8637ee93997845fe7856013ddf80bbbf6faa8559d2416f05f41bda15c3b0694" "q-5984/selection/f9d04c9c9aebd95d4a5851eca34c20e710d86597253d39199142f142ece1434f" "q-5984/selection/f49e5f4b6fe6e1c12a4d7501c2392108e0d059370f9e53e2fc0e117cf664fa60" "q-5984/selection/fe02abcadda6602139249542e8243f50894f0a42aacae4c0c9af2555f94d3639"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5984" :question/id #uuid "9fad5ced-1622-5289-8903-0b749a22e8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-5984" :question/problem "The length of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ on $[2,4]$ is given by" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=2{x}^{2},$ $a=2,$ and $b=4.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=4x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+(4x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-5984/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327/selection/e50a63ded87e61a7c75a01e50b4c5fedfc3bcc24bf622dd94f8e2bd3052343d5" :answer/id #uuid "5056685c-72c9-521e-8e1a-d9f478a23a69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327/selection/61ec1e9de4cc5268f8d1cbe7fc74a4615b6fd618362088bb3fa02ba5198b8be3" :answer/id #uuid "08b6f25a-e9e9-59bd-9947-9ff12f815bb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327/selection/5fa875f8870695b5d46b3d3dbd9ff341b52c0ba1db409473b496a511ad5dc06a" :answer/id #uuid "d0707116-ef74-5197-963c-8c375cacd1cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+2{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327/selection/bd3bddd0c47812603903a30fa2d35399c518f34c4e6c23bb4c4e52552fcf31b3" :answer/id #uuid "e8eb275b-2f62-5869-988c-ba551a60558a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327/selection/258d059782bf9463d52398e70dcfdb00e02f14659e96139d6d9f4eb225858b28" :answer/id #uuid "14180a72-795d-5d8c-8111-279d202e86e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01c8dc1d-a7d1-5f5d-b2d8-5a99fecec513" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15327/selection/258d059782bf9463d52398e70dcfdb00e02f14659e96139d6d9f4eb225858b28" :answer-field/choices ["q-15327/selection/e50a63ded87e61a7c75a01e50b4c5fedfc3bcc24bf622dd94f8e2bd3052343d5" "q-15327/selection/61ec1e9de4cc5268f8d1cbe7fc74a4615b6fd618362088bb3fa02ba5198b8be3" "q-15327/selection/5fa875f8870695b5d46b3d3dbd9ff341b52c0ba1db409473b496a511ad5dc06a" "q-15327/selection/bd3bddd0c47812603903a30fa2d35399c518f34c4e6c23bb4c4e52552fcf31b3" "q-15327/selection/258d059782bf9463d52398e70dcfdb00e02f14659e96139d6d9f4eb225858b28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15327" :question/id #uuid "e867f4c1-a3f1-54bb-a1ef-62ea49513b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-15327" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/assets/431975da27fb1ff06baa520ef4f870cb34c879f384bfc5ddd774422f15fe7b57.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve $y=4{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}$ on $[0,2],$ as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=4{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4},$ $a=0,$ and $b=2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4(\\frac{-2x}{4}){e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}=-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{(-2x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/4})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-15327/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15327"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-15397"] :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)$ on $[1,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x),$ $a=1,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{(-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\sqrt{{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote, that we use $|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$, which is valid due to that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x>0$ on $[1,3].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999/selection/07782147568457e65bf72b39b1dfd68e0147502c2984a5895620cf1c76ddaa45" :answer/id #uuid "f036e676-2b35-52a1-9ece-1e6a06bc2889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{1+(1+x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999/selection/8397ab75b73f7a227369205487aac6bcc7fc9db753554dbdbd50cd5fbf16f6ea" :answer/id #uuid "441ab2bf-09a0-5257-9d8e-74852f1be1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999/selection/107d4bf1512bd858b4b44952cbcbe5467068b43498ca192271ac28e8b38bfc76" :answer/id #uuid "4e3d5187-5b96-5fcf-9628-3d6ac3506ac6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999/selection/0c6ca2506e80d03ea039f35e741e106de901e7eaa79c9a3e3963f0a77c56367e" :answer/id #uuid "aca3fca6-5cf0-5b68-978f-afe59779aa73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x-1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999/selection/1e2e53a3c29df78d782b11ee25ae5b8e6059933274d246210dafaf175766ccbf" :answer/id #uuid "e300d736-562b-587a-aebb-407e924a77d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1622dfed-9906-5dab-b116-6b52f69f162e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-5999/selection/1e2e53a3c29df78d782b11ee25ae5b8e6059933274d246210dafaf175766ccbf" :answer-field/choices ["q-5999/selection/07782147568457e65bf72b39b1dfd68e0147502c2984a5895620cf1c76ddaa45" "q-5999/selection/8397ab75b73f7a227369205487aac6bcc7fc9db753554dbdbd50cd5fbf16f6ea" "q-5999/selection/107d4bf1512bd858b4b44952cbcbe5467068b43498ca192271ac28e8b38bfc76" "q-5999/selection/0c6ca2506e80d03ea039f35e741e106de901e7eaa79c9a3e3963f0a77c56367e" "q-5999/selection/1e2e53a3c29df78d782b11ee25ae5b8e6059933274d246210dafaf175766ccbf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5999" :question/id #uuid "a117ce46-57bd-500d-84af-8369732dd17e" :question/math-academy-id "q-5999" :question/problem "The length of the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x$ on $[2,6]$ is given by" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x,$ $a=2,$ and $b=6.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-x+1=1-x\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)=1-x$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{1+(1-x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-5999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "965026e6-db46-5930-8844-c423e6ea795a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346846/field-1/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "020b498d-a6f3-5d0e-8bcc-c4d1314160b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346846/field-1/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d" :answer/id #uuid "67434fb4-5dc3-5d30-bb28-a614c8e4d1da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346846/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "55985c38-3501-5c26-9909-0e2c44ca6dff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346846/field-1/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer-field/choices ["q-346846/field-1/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-346846/field-1/d472470bf61b62667bf520b42074414f07d1266def1002f8f8325fe27d872b2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346846" :question/id #uuid "931269a7-495c-5a1a-9a6c-8781a5275593" :question/math-academy-id "q-346846" :question/problem "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\frac{1}{3}{({x}^{2}+2)}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [2,5].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{({x}^{2}+2)}^{3/2},$ $a=2,$ and $b=5.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{({x}^{2}+2)}^{1/2}\\cdot 2x=x\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+2)}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[x\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+2)}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}={x}^{2}+1$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x)|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(5)^{3}+(5)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3}+(2)] \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346846/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362546/field-1/cdd11741e7067347debe09916ae5a9baa45ad671d02aa65fcb6f61bea7e0cdeb" :answer/id #uuid "9c7c219e-c126-57ee-bcda-4a9b40d1de4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362546/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "674e8d2d-7ebb-5670-a1cb-802f3074ddab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362546/field-1/cdd11741e7067347debe09916ae5a9baa45ad671d02aa65fcb6f61bea7e0cdeb" :answer-field/choices ["q-362546/field-1/cdd11741e7067347debe09916ae5a9baa45ad671d02aa65fcb6f61bea7e0cdeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362546" :question/id #uuid "2b9cd37d-14b9-5aad-8145-b36356967776" :question/math-academy-id "q-362546" :question/problem "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}$ for $x\\in [0,1].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},$ $a=0,$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(2-{x}^{2})^{-1/2}(-2x)=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2-{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}}{2-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}}))|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})]-[\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{2}})] \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-362546/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-362589/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "8ea35659-49ee-5af8-9718-886025424254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362589/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8868de0f-8eec-58d3-ad15-a3d7198a4523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-362589/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1db34eb-a69c-55c2-bc49-7426f9137050" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-362589/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-362589/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-362589/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-362589" :question/id #uuid "e4fdd583-dc77-5faa-9875-6977242c4205" :question/math-academy-id "q-362589" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ for $x\\in [-1,1].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ $a=-1,$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}=\\frac{1-x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1-x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{(1-x)^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+1-2x+{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2-2x}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2(1-x)}{(1-x)(1+x)}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1+x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1+x}}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{1+x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{1+x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1+x}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1+1}-2\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{1+(-1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}(\\sqrt{2})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-362589/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-362589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352925/field-1/e945c90bb407e9e064b0135a884310e690b0673e7e9151d4294101792ac2c3b3" :answer/id #uuid "c4bf2e86-1ac0-50ad-a9d3-3a26e4b49ce1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^3-e^{-3}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352925/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd960b61-2dd2-5cdf-aae2-fb036f4e55a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352925/field-1/e945c90bb407e9e064b0135a884310e690b0673e7e9151d4294101792ac2c3b3" :answer-field/choices ["q-352925/field-1/e945c90bb407e9e064b0135a884310e690b0673e7e9151d4294101792ac2c3b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352925" :question/id #uuid "08fee865-501b-5e99-8db0-650bb5d40ada" :question/math-academy-id "q-352925" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{6}$ for $x\\in [0,1].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{6},$ $a=0,$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{e}^{3x}-{e}^{-3x}}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{{e}^{3x}-{e}^{-3x}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{e}^{6x}-2+{e}^{-6x}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{e}^{6x}+2+{e}^{-6x}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{({e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x})^{2}}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{e}^{3x}+{e}^{-3x}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{e}^{3x}-{e}^{-3x}}{6})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{3(1)}-{e}^{-3(1)}}{6}]-[\\frac{{e}^{3(0)}-{e}^{-3(0)}}{6}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6}-1}{6{e}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352925/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352925"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer/id #uuid "22105719-c899-52ae-9cb0-c74ffdd3f608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997/selection/adb728599602a1a3a50484f34a901ee3faaa5562325b61d23044fdd525aadbb3" :answer/id #uuid "5a1ca712-5ccc-5b34-830b-34af75b427f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{34}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer/id #uuid "742af504-b01c-5e63-9e30-f19aef6413c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" :answer/id #uuid "c3ceeacd-1a70-569d-b48f-91ef53c9d40a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "5515087e-d44f-572c-aa96-c81caf09d1bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b961aa-3d15-5f1f-8727-2276da010610" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-5997/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" :answer-field/choices ["q-5997/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" "q-5997/selection/adb728599602a1a3a50484f34a901ee3faaa5562325b61d23044fdd525aadbb3" "q-5997/selection/5521c093c4d60c23d630a99bc791ac7318f4615e164361df756510ffc0408a97" "q-5997/selection/bcbe057cec11b06e556ce6eb64efebcbc7b9b530f339b3d67669620f3e550dc2" "q-5997/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-5997" :question/id #uuid "a835d9c7-8f8c-5cd5-a5d7-d053a9a2c3f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-5997" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=3.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={x}^{1/2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${f}^{′}(x)={x}^{1/2}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{({x}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{3}{(1+x)}^{3/2}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[{4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-5997/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622/selection/5eb48b177ed6f2628e25a696562dc42d9f7d038bbf02faed9f137cc2fb36cf52" :answer/id #uuid "00c9f1aa-fa4f-5572-a3ee-683810dd45dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622/selection/ad41046bdceb880acf03be1d6ffa713850fbcfed9477044f1d14311e99a55902" :answer/id #uuid "a639978a-82f2-5159-a9b5-b89411e3c9a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622/selection/81d34d2f414a35227e6b61422db069ca0d9d472b6308350d712a19ab7dc46974" :answer/id #uuid "3bda05f6-e286-575c-9852-cd43ce45b3de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{x+1}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622/selection/a3b0934bd7123c19c340bf9807be9f6ead3d43f5936fc584a24f364cee15a03b" :answer/id #uuid "ed3c2010-7a09-57f2-8a36-b6e5d81aea9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622/selection/6e6cf2fd57c8e042f7fe72ff1544dffaa53ba1ea10bb64b977a6df6127f062c0" :answer/id #uuid "545b6deb-4afb-5001-8230-6d71c32fc783" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03e09677-8391-531e-bfc0-2ab338d6fe41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82622/selection/81d34d2f414a35227e6b61422db069ca0d9d472b6308350d712a19ab7dc46974" :answer-field/choices ["q-82622/selection/5eb48b177ed6f2628e25a696562dc42d9f7d038bbf02faed9f137cc2fb36cf52" "q-82622/selection/ad41046bdceb880acf03be1d6ffa713850fbcfed9477044f1d14311e99a55902" "q-82622/selection/81d34d2f414a35227e6b61422db069ca0d9d472b6308350d712a19ab7dc46974" "q-82622/selection/a3b0934bd7123c19c340bf9807be9f6ead3d43f5936fc584a24f364cee15a03b" "q-82622/selection/6e6cf2fd57c8e042f7fe72ff1544dffaa53ba1ea10bb64b977a6df6127f062c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82622" :question/id #uuid "debe9b7a-8c8d-5eda-bcc5-c138c3db9537" :question/math-academy-id "q-82622" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4x+4}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{4x+4}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{x+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\sqrt{x+1}+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82622/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82622"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003/selection/44d1056735481c66859961ee861e62bad45a6681e8313cc19c1ee23156ca039f" :answer/id #uuid "425f803d-de1c-5a31-9348-7f5f474df2ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{2-x}+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003/selection/8cfc67c98a1cb18fb7cf8fd703b76960d1574a5203c2ef2487538b99197bf02d" :answer/id #uuid "23259fe4-6729-5e8d-b710-22f8a82fbec8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003/selection/2c9da74c8aa0ec2c82cb0cda0a413471543ebd3f84d4c764b1c72240cf53cac4" :answer/id #uuid "0cbf1d97-af21-5ce8-9db7-0e7e6d0dd02b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-3\\sqrt{2-x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003/selection/56a60582be7fc9e2432c15286152fff2894c37bf4d14f83da5631de4d5bdb577" :answer/id #uuid "289689a7-6d13-5736-89c1-c8f6fa89b554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003/selection/61e300b52145593c200e1ab8a0868d716a245f7f15d82f5085dc5a779658b655" :answer/id #uuid "a571a3cd-402d-5d2b-9ae3-5fb4210f78d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}-x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3c78f87-61b8-5747-a282-bde57adaa918" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-6003/selection/8cfc67c98a1cb18fb7cf8fd703b76960d1574a5203c2ef2487538b99197bf02d" :answer-field/choices ["q-6003/selection/44d1056735481c66859961ee861e62bad45a6681e8313cc19c1ee23156ca039f" "q-6003/selection/8cfc67c98a1cb18fb7cf8fd703b76960d1574a5203c2ef2487538b99197bf02d" "q-6003/selection/2c9da74c8aa0ec2c82cb0cda0a413471543ebd3f84d4c764b1c72240cf53cac4" "q-6003/selection/56a60582be7fc9e2432c15286152fff2894c37bf4d14f83da5631de4d5bdb577" "q-6003/selection/61e300b52145593c200e1ab8a0868d716a245f7f15d82f5085dc5a779658b655"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6003" :question/id #uuid "ecf6b6f7-3aff-5153-b0cd-275806dc9892" :question/math-academy-id "q-6003" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm (-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}+\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-6003/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6003"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-82624"] :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2+4{x}^{2}-4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2+4{x}^{2}-4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=4{x}^{2}-4x+1=(2x-1)^{2}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm (2x-1).\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int (2x-1)\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm ({x}^{2}-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y={x}^{2}-x+4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612/selection/e805c367590d5902b11942cff1bfa3e834e53cabaab4e9eae7ccc289a46f2a7a" :answer/id #uuid "6d53298e-e728-5d04-895c-1303f03d0dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612/selection/7984ac9080e351ce059ed627421ddfa071cf14d836bacc279ec5626f90ffb60d" :answer/id #uuid "f1f10d36-492a-55a8-a0ff-7ccbf12bf27e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612/selection/bac81ff485c0c0097777daf8fd48a0932473c84e9a5c57ba288b7f5eb447213d" :answer/id #uuid "8878c1a5-fa8c-57ef-9556-c24e82e1c33b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2+{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612/selection/d51dc5027e95be966976c07c71c42be3b0fff67c8232b486fe9e93e172b83258" :answer/id #uuid "bed3dc3f-ac05-5ac0-8a5a-c6cf94d4b4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4+{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612/selection/f4ff1d7a14ca1b3b7213f41e6a85ffb1fb52b192a874cd0e552b048c5c0b99a5" :answer/id #uuid "b4331cce-1be3-52b0-b625-6e14ccd6310c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "58d91d7b-7308-539a-b5b5-d0a7e830b25c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82612/selection/e805c367590d5902b11942cff1bfa3e834e53cabaab4e9eae7ccc289a46f2a7a" :answer-field/choices ["q-82612/selection/e805c367590d5902b11942cff1bfa3e834e53cabaab4e9eae7ccc289a46f2a7a" "q-82612/selection/7984ac9080e351ce059ed627421ddfa071cf14d836bacc279ec5626f90ffb60d" "q-82612/selection/bac81ff485c0c0097777daf8fd48a0932473c84e9a5c57ba288b7f5eb447213d" "q-82612/selection/d51dc5027e95be966976c07c71c42be3b0fff67c8232b486fe9e93e172b83258" "q-82612/selection/f4ff1d7a14ca1b3b7213f41e6a85ffb1fb52b192a874cd0e552b048c5c0b99a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82612" :question/id #uuid "1b05c5c4-2217-5350-94dd-be0220e8c600" :question/math-academy-id "q-82612" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}={cos}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82612/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615/selection/124635f062cb29ef571241f62186342e5ca7e89b9a50e381135c40bb2fcf45b4" :answer/id #uuid "497c0c31-1c23-5072-a25f-91b03bb2ded3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(4x)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615/selection/4298fc94efb8e485b9ce2c6ab5c17c6c331d1d8e345d748251efdf4449efee8b" :answer/id #uuid "dfcb29c1-0ed0-54e3-bb56-70f8288055ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615/selection/1aa34971813a36ad8981b164d4af2b5ac8439c11e2f150f85f3836209f9e65d7" :answer/id #uuid "58310cad-4b3d-5b2a-92ef-a3f61859ea16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{sec}^{2}⁡(2x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615/selection/712f03563a2dd13b17930763d69fa68033ef6564baeb8fc7e411dade8781407e" :answer/id #uuid "2f88ac32-668d-59bd-91f0-4b1f208bc85b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{tan}^{2}⁡(2x)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615/selection/40435fa5f4450584f336ad78568cfa63b4076fa1cc503289340fcc993d5e1140" :answer/id #uuid "72d1741f-2f12-56f8-825c-63e9baddf4c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e1660e-6bb7-558c-a5e4-d5db08b6b790" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82615/selection/40435fa5f4450584f336ad78568cfa63b4076fa1cc503289340fcc993d5e1140" :answer-field/choices ["q-82615/selection/124635f062cb29ef571241f62186342e5ca7e89b9a50e381135c40bb2fcf45b4" "q-82615/selection/4298fc94efb8e485b9ce2c6ab5c17c6c331d1d8e345d748251efdf4449efee8b" "q-82615/selection/1aa34971813a36ad8981b164d4af2b5ac8439c11e2f150f85f3836209f9e65d7" "q-82615/selection/712f03563a2dd13b17930763d69fa68033ef6564baeb8fc7e411dade8781407e" "q-82615/selection/40435fa5f4450584f336ad78568cfa63b4076fa1cc503289340fcc993d5e1140"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82615" :question/id #uuid "e5d5028e-993e-5a50-9b51-1e2b2f23dd9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-82615" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+4{sec}^{4}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\sqrt{1+4{sec}^{4}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=4{sec}^{4}⁡(2x)\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm 2{sec}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm 2\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(2x)\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-82615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55f783c4-25d6-5855-877e-31bed16b12c4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7268"] :question/problem "What is the arc length of the curve $y = \\arccos{x}$ on $\\left[0,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right]?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int _a^b \\sqrt{1 + [f'(x)]^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)= \\arccos{x} ,$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\dfrac{1}{2}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nf'(x) =-\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f'(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{\\frac{2-{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-560"] :question/problem "Compute the arc length of  the curve $y=x^{3/2}$ between the points $x=0$ and $x=\\dfrac{4}{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/assets/4ed8b94a4fff3c22697264e467f955f2e51a62618d03295c4e4f38493bff2ced.png)" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int _a^b \\sqrt{1 + [f'(x)]^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)= x^{3/2},$ $a=0,$ and $b=\\dfrac{4}{3}.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nf'(x) =   \\dfrac{3}{2}x^{1/2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt { 1 + [f'(x)]^2 }\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{9}{4}x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4+9x}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}(4+9x)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}}\\sqrt{4+9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{4+9x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt { 1 + [f'(x)]^2 } = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sqrt{4 + 9x}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+{[{f}^{′}(x)]}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\sqrt{4+9x}\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate this integral using the substitution $u= 4+9x.$ Then, $\\textrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{9}\\textrm{d}u.$\n\nWe also need to compute new limits:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ u & 4 & 16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\sqrt{4+9x}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{16}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{\\int }_{4}^{16}{u}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{[\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{\\frac{3}{2}}]}_{4}^{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{[{u}^{\\frac{3}{2}}]}_{4}^{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}([(16)^{\\frac{3}{2}}]-[(4)^{\\frac{3}{2}}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}([64]-[8]) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-561"] :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\displaystyle  \\int_{5}^{6} } \\sqrt{1+\\dfrac {x^2}{x^2-16}}  \\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve? \n\n- $y=  \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2-16}}$\n\n- $y=  \\sqrt{x^2-16} + \\sqrt 5$\n\n- $y=  \\dfrac{x}{x^2-16} + 1$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int _a^b \\sqrt{1 + [f'(x)]^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL=\\int_{5}^{6}  \\sqrt{1+\\dfrac {x^2}{x^2-16}}  \\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[f'(x)]^2=\\dfrac {x^2}{x^2-16}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad f'(x) = \\pm \\dfrac {x}{\\sqrt{x^2-16}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-16}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=  \\sqrt{x^2-16} + \\sqrt 5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
